            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-4032-Python",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-4032 high vulnerability for Python package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The ÔÇ£ipaddressÔÇØ module contained incorrect information about whether certain IPv4 and IPv6 addresses were designated as ÔÇ£globally reachableÔÇØ or ÔÇ£privateÔÇØ. This affected the is_private and is_global properties of the ipaddress.IPv4Address, ipaddress.IPv4Network, ipaddress.IPv6Address, and ipaddress.IPv6Network classes, where values wouldnÔÇÖt be returned in accordance with the latest information from the IANA Special-Purpose Address Registries.\n\nCPython 3.12.4 and 3.13.0a6 contain updated information from these registries and thus have the intended behavior."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-4032\nSeverity: high\nPackage: Python\nVersion: 3.12.3\nFix Version: 3.8.20,3.9.20,3.10.15,3.11.10,3.12.4,3.13.0a6\nType: binary\nLocation: /app/.venv/Scripts/python.exe\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2024-4032](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-4032)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-4032**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | Python  | 3.12.3  | 3.8.20,3.9.20,3.10.15,3.11.10,3.12.4,3.13.0a6  | binary  | /app/.venv/Scripts/python.exe  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2024-4032](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-4032)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-0938-Python",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-0938 medium vulnerability for Python package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The Python standard library functions `urllib.parse.urlsplit` and `urlparse` accepted domain names that included square brackets which isn't valid according to RFC 3986. Square brackets are only meant to be used as delimiters for specifying IPv6 and IPvFuture hosts in URLs. This could result in differential parsing across the Python URL parser and other specification-compliant URL parsers."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-0938\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: Python\nVersion: 3.12.3\nFix Version: 3.9.22,3.10.17,3.11.12,3.12.9,3.13.2,3.14.0a5\nType: binary\nLocation: /app/.venv/Scripts/pythonw.exe\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2025-0938](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-0938)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-0938**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | Python  | 3.12.3  | 3.9.22,3.10.17,3.11.12,3.12.9,3.13.2,3.14.0a5  | binary  | /app/.venv/Scripts/pythonw.exe  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2025-0938](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-0938)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "6.3"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-7592-Python",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-7592 high vulnerability for Python package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "There is a LOW severity vulnerability affecting CPython, specifically the\n'http.cookies' standard library module.\n\n\nWhen parsing cookies that contained backslashes for quoted characters in\nthe cookie value, the parser would use an algorithm with quadratic\ncomplexity, resulting in excess CPU resources being used while parsing the\nvalue."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-7592\nSeverity: high\nPackage: Python\nVersion: 3.12.3\nFix Version: 3.8.20,3.9.20,3.10.15,3.11.10,3.12.6,3.13.0rc2\nType: binary\nLocation: /app/.venv/Scripts/python.exe\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2024-7592](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-7592)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-7592**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | Python  | 3.12.3  | 3.8.20,3.9.20,3.10.15,3.11.10,3.12.6,3.13.0rc2  | binary  | /app/.venv/Scripts/python.exe  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2024-7592](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-7592)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-12254-Python",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-12254 high vulnerability for Python package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Starting in Python 3.12.0, the asyncio._SelectorSocketTransport.writelines()\n method would not \"pause\" writing and signal to the Protocol to drain \nthe buffer to the wire once the write buffer reached the \"high-water \nmark\". Because of this, Protocols would not periodically drain the write\n buffer potentially leading to memory exhaustion.\n\n\n\n\n\nThis\n vulnerability likely impacts a small number of users, you must be using\n Python 3.12.0 or later, on macOS or Linux, using the asyncio module \nwith protocols, and using .writelines() method which had new \nzero-copy-on-write behavior in Python 3.12.0 and later. If not all of \nthese factors are true then your usage of Python is unaffected."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-12254\nSeverity: high\nPackage: Python\nVersion: 3.12.3\nFix Version: 3.12.9,3.13.2,3.14.0a3\nType: binary\nLocation: /app/.venv/Scripts/pythonw.exe\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2024-12254](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-12254)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-12254**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | Python  | 3.12.3  | 3.12.9,3.13.2,3.14.0a3  | binary  | /app/.venv/Scripts/pythonw.exe  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2024-12254](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-12254)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "8.7"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2011-3389-libgnutls30t64",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2011-3389 low vulnerability for libgnutls30t64 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The SSL protocol, as used in certain configurations in Microsoft Windows and Microsoft Internet Explorer, Mozilla Firefox, Google Chrome, Opera, and other products, encrypts data by using CBC mode with chained initialization vectors, which allows man-in-the-middle attackers to obtain plaintext HTTP headers via a blockwise chosen-boundary attack (BCBA) on an HTTPS session, in conjunction with JavaScript code that uses (1) the HTML5 WebSocket API, (2) the Java URLConnection API, or (3) the Silverlight WebClient API, aka a \"BEAST\" attack."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2011-3389\nSeverity: low\nPackage: libgnutls30t64\nVersion: 3.8.9-3\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:13\nLink: [CVE-2011-3389](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2011-3389)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2011-3389**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| low  | libgnutls30t64  | 3.8.9-3  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:13  | [CVE-2011-3389](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2011-3389)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libgnutls30t64@3.8.9-3?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian-13\u0026upstream=gnutls28"
                ],
                "security-severity": "4.3"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-8088-Python",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-8088 high vulnerability for Python package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "There is a HIGH severity vulnerability affecting the CPython \"zipfile\"\nmodule affecting \"zipfile.Path\". Note that the more common API \"zipfile.ZipFile\" class is unaffected.\n\n\n\n\n\nWhen iterating over names of entries in a zip archive (for example, methods\nof \"zipfile.Path\" like \"namelist()\", \"iterdir()\", etc)\nthe process can be put into an infinite loop with a maliciously crafted\nzip archive. This defect applies when reading only metadata or extracting\nthe contents of the zip archive. Programs that are not handling\nuser-controlled zip archives are not affected."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-8088\nSeverity: high\nPackage: Python\nVersion: 3.12.3\nFix Version: 3.8.20,3.9.20,3.10.15,3.11.10,3.12.6,3.13.0rc2\nType: binary\nLocation: /app/.venv/Scripts/pythonw.exe\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2024-8088](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-8088)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-8088**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | Python  | 3.12.3  | 3.8.20,3.9.20,3.10.15,3.11.10,3.12.6,3.13.0rc2  | binary  | /app/.venv/Scripts/pythonw.exe  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2024-8088](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-8088)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "8.7"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-8194-Python",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-8194 high vulnerability for Python package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "There is a defect in the CPython ÔÇ£tarfileÔÇØ module affecting the ÔÇ£TarFileÔÇØ extraction and entry enumeration APIs. The tar implementation would process tar archives with negative offsets without error, resulting in an infinite loop and deadlock during the parsing of maliciously crafted tar archives. \n\nThis vulnerability can be mitigated by including the following patch after importing the ÔÇ£tarfileÔÇØ module:┬á https://gist.github.com/sethmlarson/1716ac5b82b73dbcbf23ad2eff8b33e1"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-8194\nSeverity: high\nPackage: Python\nVersion: 3.12.3\nFix Version: 3.9.24,3.10.19,3.11.14,3.12.12,3.13.6,3.14.0rc2\nType: binary\nLocation: /app/.venv/Scripts/python.exe\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2025-8194](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-8194)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-8194**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | Python  | 3.12.3  | 3.9.24,3.10.19,3.11.14,3.12.12,3.13.6,3.14.0rc2  | binary  | /app/.venv/Scripts/python.exe  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2025-8194](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-8194)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-6923-Python",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-6923 medium vulnerability for Python package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "There is a MEDIUM severity vulnerability affecting CPython.\n\nThe \nemail module didnÔÇÖt properly quote newlines for email headers when \nserializing an email message allowing for header injection when an email\n is serialized."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-6923\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: Python\nVersion: 3.12.3\nFix Version: 3.8.20,3.9.20,3.10.15,3.11.10,3.12.5,3.13.0rc2\nType: binary\nLocation: /app/.venv/Scripts/python.exe\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2024-6923](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-6923)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-6923**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | Python  | 3.12.3  | 3.8.20,3.9.20,3.10.15,3.11.10,3.12.5,3.13.0rc2  | binary  | /app/.venv/Scripts/python.exe  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2024-6923](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-6923)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
