            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-4330-Python",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-4330 high vulnerability for Python package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Allows the extraction filter to be ignored, allowing symlink targets to point outside the destination directory, and the modification of some file metadata.\n\n\nYou are affected by this vulnerability if using the tarfile┬ámodule to extract untrusted tar archives using TarFile.extractall()┬áor TarFile.extract()┬áusing the filter=┬áparameter with a value of \"data\"┬áor \"tar\". See the tarfile  extraction filters documentation https://docs.python.org/3/library/tarfile.html#tarfile-extraction-filter ┬áfor more information.\n\nNote that for Python 3.14 or later the default value of filter=┬áchanged from \"no filtering\" to `\"data\", so if you are relying on this new default behavior then your usage is also affected.\n\nNote that none of these vulnerabilities significantly affect the installation of source distributions which are tar archives as source distributions already allow arbitrary code execution during the build process. However when evaluating source distributions it's important to avoid installing source distributions with suspicious links."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-4330\nSeverity: high\nPackage: Python\nVersion: 3.12.3\nFix Version: 3.9.23,3.10.18,3.11.13,3.12.11,3.13.4,3.14.0b3\nType: binary\nLocation: /app/.venv/Scripts/pythonw.exe\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2025-4330](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-4330)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-4330**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | Python  | 3.12.3  | 3.9.23,3.10.18,3.11.13,3.12.11,3.13.4,3.14.0b3  | binary  | /app/.venv/Scripts/pythonw.exe  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2025-4330](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-4330)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2018-20796-libc-bin",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2018-20796 low vulnerability for libc-bin package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the GNU C Library (aka glibc or libc6) through 2.29, check_dst_limits_calc_pos_1 in posix/regexec.c has Uncontrolled Recursion, as demonstrated by '(\\227|)(\\\\1\\\\1|t1|\\\\\\2537)+' in grep."
              },
