            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-12718-Python",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-12718 medium vulnerability for Python package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Allows modifying some file metadata (e.g. last modified) with filter=\"data\"┬áor file permissions (chmod) with filter=\"tar\"┬áof files outside the extraction directory.\nYou are affected by this vulnerability if using the tarfile┬ámodule to extract untrusted tar archives using TarFile.extractall()┬áor TarFile.extract()┬áusing the filter=┬áparameter with a value of \"data\"┬áor \"tar\". See the tarfile  extraction filters documentation https://docs.python.org/3/library/tarfile.html#tarfile-extraction-filter ┬áfor more information. Only Python versions 3.12 or later are affected by these vulnerabilities, earlier versions don't include the extraction filter feature.\n\nNote that for Python 3.14 or later the default value of filter=┬áchanged from \"no filtering\" to `\"data\", so if you are relying on this new default behavior then your usage is also affected.\n\nNote that none of these vulnerabilities significantly affect the installation of source distributions which are tar archives as source distributions already allow arbitrary code execution during the build process. However when evaluating source distributions it's important to avoid installing source distributions with suspicious links."
              },
