            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-4517-Python",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-4517 critical vulnerability for Python package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Allows arbitrary filesystem writes outside the extraction directory during extraction with filter=\"data\".\n\n\nYou are affected by this vulnerability if using the tarfile┬ámodule to extract untrusted tar archives using TarFile.extractall()┬áor TarFile.extract()┬áusing the filter=┬áparameter with a value of \"data\"┬áor \"tar\". See the tarfile  extraction filters documentation https://docs.python.org/3/library/tarfile.html#tarfile-extraction-filter ┬áfor more information.\n\nNote that for Python 3.14 or later the default value of filter=┬áchanged from \"no filtering\" to `\"data\", so if you are relying on this new default behavior then your usage is also affected.\n\nNote that none of these vulnerabilities significantly affect the installation of source distributions which are tar archives as source distributions already allow arbitrary code execution during the build process. However when evaluating source distributions it's important to avoid installing source distributions with suspicious links."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-4517\nSeverity: critical\nPackage: Python\nVersion: 3.12.3\nFix Version: 3.9.23,3.10.18,3.11.13,3.12.11,3.13.4,3.14.0b3\nType: binary\nLocation: /app/.venv/Scripts/pythonw.exe\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2025-4517](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-4517)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-4517**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| critical  | Python  | 3.12.3  | 3.9.23,3.10.18,3.11.13,3.12.11,3.13.4,3.14.0b3  | binary  | /app/.venv/Scripts/pythonw.exe  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2025-4517](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-4517)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "9.4"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-13836-Python",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-13836 medium vulnerability for Python package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When reading an HTTP response from a server, if no read amount is specified, the default behavior will be to use Content-Length. This allows a malicious server to cause the client to read large amounts of data into memory, potentially causing OOM or other DoS."
